**This task has two halves and is not done until both are.**

**Half 1 — validate Phase 1 for real.** Not "the PRs merged" — evidence that the flow works end to end:

- a push to `development` on policy-service and policy-console builds under the sandbox image names (`bridge-policy/service-sandbox`, `bridge-policy/console-sandbox`) and touches no master-stream image;
- the build writes the `_sandbox`-suffixed manifest keys, and `manifest_conf` kept every one of them (a key missing from `manifest_conf` is silently pruned — evidence E12);
- master-stream environments are unaffected: no deploy fired on any environment other than cto-dev-kpr;
- on cto-dev-kpr the `policy-sandbox` ArgoCD Application is healthy, `policy.yaml` is **gone** from `bdg-eng-tops-techops-argocd-pipeline/applications/cto-dev-kpr/templates/`, and only one Application owns namespace `policy` (two would prune each other — evidence E18);
- the four `manifest_conf` components are all present on the environment, including `agentvisorsample` and `adapterservice`, which the base chart defaults to `false` (evidence E16);
- the sandbox chart still renders byte-identical to the original modulo name and image keys (the drift guard).

Record the evidence in `docs/evidence.md` and mark PLAN.md §5 Step 5 done.

**Half 2 — turn the DRAFT tasks into real ones.** Every Phase 2 (KAIF) and Phase 3 (POA) task was written from PLAN.md §9 *before* anything was proven. Go through each one and:

- replace every `TO CONFIRM` with the answer, or promote it to a blocking question for that phase;
- fold in every lesson Phase 1 taught that §9 does not yet say — and update §9 itself, since it is the reusable recipe and must stay application-agnostic;
- correct the order, the repo names, and the per-step acceptance criteria;
- drop the `DRAFT ·` prefix from each task title as it becomes real work.

Do not start Phase 2 before this task is Complete. The whole point of the phasing is that KAIF inherits a proven recipe instead of a plausible one.
